<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 30,102 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 30,102 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 30,102 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 77,353 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Monday	September 14</p>
<p>    Export cargo			     771	1,625</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  29,331     75,728</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, five were expected to sail and five were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>The port observed public holiday on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  74,000	 Chesa Peak City    16/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
